{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And on the eighth day he shall be circumcised.</b> On the day, even on Sabbath, and specifically a definite circumcision, such as one born on Sabbath eve or on the day of Sabbath. But a doubtful circumcision, such as one born on Sabbath eve during twilight, at a time that is doubtful whether day or night — they do not circumcise him until the first day, which is the tenth. For thus the Sages said: an infant may be circumcised at eight, at nine, at ten, at eleven, at twelve — no less and no more. As is its normal course, at eight; born during twilight on other days of the year, at nine; born during twilight on Sabbath eve, circumcised at ten; a festival after Sabbath, at eleven; two festival days of Rosh HaShanah, circumcised at twelve. If he was sick, they postpone until he heals." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> Turnus Rufus the wicked asked Rabbi Akiva: Which deeds are more beautiful, those of the Holy One, blessed be He, or those of flesh and blood? He said to him: Those of flesh and blood. Turnus Rufus said: Behold the heavens and the earth — can a person make the likes of them? Rabbi Akiva said to him: Do not speak to me about what is above, over which creatures have no dominion; rather, speak of things found among human beings. He said to him: Why do you circumcise? He said: Indeed I knew that about this matter you were going to ask me, and therefore I prefaced for you that the deeds of flesh and blood are more beautiful than those of the Holy One, blessed be He. He brought him stalks and cakes and said to him: These are the deed of the Holy One, blessed be He, and these are the deed of flesh and blood. Turnus Rufus said to him: If He desires circumcision, why does the child not emerge circumcised from his mother's womb? Rabbi Akiva said to him: And why does its umbilical cord emerge with him, attached to his belly, and his mother cuts it? And as for what you say — why does he not emerge circumcised — it is because the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the commandments only to refine Israel through them, as it is said (Proverbs 30:5): ״כל אמרת אלוה צרופה״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:04.311232123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}